      "script": "",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": true,
        "locked": true,
        "style": "transparent",
        "text": "A tokenizer splits text into subword units learned by byte-pair encoding, which merges the commonest adjacent pairs over and over. Frequent words survive whole while rare ones shatter, and a leading space usually belongs to the token after it.\n\nThe model never sees letters, so counting the r’s in a word asks it about something it was never given.",
